From 700dd6927d0b02da720ca5ff9153ffc6e5a15e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:18:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Mass matrices of simplices by kernels, profiling of the L2
 projection

- The mass matrices of the elements without a tensor basis (simplices),
  which MFEM 4.10 does not assemble on the device, are computed by a
  kernel (batch::computeMassMatrices, integration rule of
  mfem::MassIntegrator) and given to the full assembly of MFEM by an
  integrator implementing AssembleEA, when the post-processings are
  computed by kernels. The operator of the implicit gradient
  regularization of these elements is still assembled element by
  element (diffusion term).
- The regularization operator is given by the coefficient of its
  diffusion term instead of a function adding the integrators.
- Profiling sections of the L2 projection: data of the kernels,
  operator, right-hand sides, resolutions.
- PostProcessingsKernelsTest also compares the implicit gradient
  regularizations.
- Documentation: post-processings in the guide of the computations by
  batches.
